@title STORY • ZANE: WAITING WELL
@bg rahman_house_day
You're Zane Rahman. Dearborn, Sunday dinner over video call. Your mom has propped the phone against the mansaf so you can "be at the table."
Mom: Habibi, you look thin. Are they feeding you?
Zane: Mama, I'm a triple jumper. I'm supposed to be light.
Mom: You're supposed to be FED. And the girl? The artist? Did you talk to her yet?
Your little brother leans into frame. "He hasn't. He just draws her name on stuff."
Zane: I do NOT—
> [Sweet] "...I'm working up to it." -> a1
> [Bold] "I'm talking to her this week. Swear on the mansaf." -> a2
> [Good] "Mama. She's shy. I'm not rushing her." -> a3
*a1
Mom: Work faster. I'm not getting younger.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Courage 2
Mom: (gasping) You swore on the MANSAF. Now you have to.
@jump a_done
*a3
@add Patience 3
Mom goes quiet. Then she smiles the way she smiles at your dad.
Mom: That's how your father waited for me. Two years. I made him earn it.
*a_done
@bg track_stadium_day
@show coachrhodes
Coach Rhodes: RAHMAN! Hop, step, JUMP! Not hop, step, look at Alexa, jump!
The jumps group loses it. You land in the sand face-first.
@show alexa
Alexa: (from the pole vault runway, very quietly) Are you okay?
Zane: (spitting sand) Never better. Thriving.
> [Bold] "Coffee? Tomorrow? I'll have less sand on me." -> b1
> [Sweet] Make her laugh. Do a dramatic sand angel. -> b2
> [Good] Give her space. Just smile. -> b3
*b1
@add Courage 3
Alexa: (after a long pause) ...Okay.
She says it so quietly you almost miss it. You don't miss it. You run a lap you weren't assigned. Coach Rhodes lets you.
@jump end
*b2
@add Alexa_Laugh 3
She laughs. The real one. You've heard it maybe four times. You're keeping count.
@jump end
*b3
@add Patience 2
She smiles back. Small. You can work with small. Small is how everything starts.
*end
Zane Rahman jumps for a living. This year, he learns the hardest jump is the one where you wait, patiently, for someone to be ready to jump with you.
